# Canonical chat reel — proven on the trial pod (reel-chat3.mp4: 20.5s, no frame
# drops, completed cited answer). Placeholders: __OUTPUT__ __BOOT__ __QUESTION__
# Choreography rationale (see [[reel-trial-findings]]):
#  - Relative Output path (VHS 0.10 rejects unquoted absolute paths).
#  - Escape after boot dismisses the model-picker wizard into the Chat view,
#    which leaves the Ask box in NORMAL mode; Type "i" enters insert first, else
#    the leading keystrokes are eaten (e.g. "What's" -> "t's", the 'a' triggers
#    append). Both done while Hidden so the mode-switch never shows.
#  - Ask, then Hide through the cold engine-load + generation, then Show the
#    finished answer: capture happens on an idle machine, so no frame drops and
#    the reel never ends on a spinner.
#  - Ends on the fleet drawer (Ctrl+g). The old Escape+G scroll is removed: "G"
#    landed in the search box as literal text; the answer already fits on screen.
Set Shell "bash"
Set FontFamily "JetBrains Mono, Symbols Nerd Font Mono, Noto Color Emoji"
Set FontSize 28
Set Width 1400
Set Height 900
Set Padding 40
Set LetterSpacing 2
Set Theme "rose-pine-moon"
Set WindowBar Colorful
Set TypingSpeed 35ms
Set Framerate 25
Output __OUTPUT__
Hide
Type "__BOOT__"
Enter
Sleep 95s
Escape
Sleep 1500ms
Type "i"
Sleep 800ms
Show
Sleep 1800ms
Type "__QUESTION__"
Sleep 700ms
Enter
Sleep 3s
Hide
Sleep 85s
Show
Sleep 7s
Ctrl+g
Sleep 3s
